// Proves runtime/jvm/src/lox/LoxClosure.java delivers its own
// StackOverflowError to a real catchBlock — kind, message, and the "after"
// line that only runs once the catch block completes normally
// (spec/04-semantics.md's Runtime Errors table).
//
// Lives in jvm-only/, not directly in translation-probes/: the CLR backend
// (runtime/clr/src/LoxClosure.cs) raises the same ceiling fault today but,
// as of this probe, still delivers it with the wrong catchability (see
// issue #238) — a bug this probe would otherwise make every CLR
// differential run report as a new divergence. Move this probe back into
// the shared directory once #238 closes.
fun f(n) { return f(n + 1); }
try {
    f(0);
    print "no error";
} catch (e) {
    print "caught " + e.kind;
    print e.message;
}
print "after";
